<title>BELGIUM: Solvay holds dividend,plans stock split.</title>
<headline>Solvay holds dividend,plans stock split.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996 (in billions of Belgian francs unless stated):</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	  13.63  vs  12.51</p>
<p>    Net current profit     11.54  vs  12.54</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary gain  2.09  vs   0.03 loss</p>
<p>    Net dividend		 550  vs    550</p>
<p>NOTE - Solvay SA is a Belgian chemicals group. In a statement about final 1996 earnings the company said it would propose a 10-for-one stock split at an extraordinary general shareholders meeting in June. The split should take place in September 1997, it added.  </p>
<p>The company provided the following breakdown of its figures:</p>
<p>    Sales		     281.97  vs 273.35</p>
<p>    of which Europe	 187     vs 184, up two percent</p>
<p>    &quot;  &quot;   Americas	  77     vs  70, up 10 percent</p>
<p>    &quot;  &quot;   U.S.		54     vs  47, up 15 percent</p>
<p>    &quot;  &quot;   Asia-Pacific    13     vs  14, down seven percent</p>
<p>    &quot;  &quot;   MidEast Africa   5     vs   5, unchanged</p>
<p>Contribution of five business units:</p>
<p>    Unit	     Sales		 EBIT*</p>
<p>    Alkalis     81.2 vs 76.9	8.8 vs 9.7</p>
<p>    Peroxygens  16.4 vs 15.8	2.2 vs 1.5</p>
<p>    Plastics    85.0 vs 87.8	3.5 vs 8.8</p>
<p>    Processing  53.1 vs 49.1	2.5 vs 0.8</p>
<p>    Health	46.2 vs 43.9	4.3 vs 3.3</p>
<p>NOTE - * EBIT: earnings before net debt expense, taxes and non allocated items</p>
<p>As well as proposing a stock split, Solvay said the extraordinary shareholders meeting would be asked to vote on a capital increase by incorporation of 17.6 billion francs in reserves. The move would take Solvay SA's capital to 50 billion francs, it said, and was designed to bring capital more in line with equity.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
